# C++ quality gates

When you add or edit C or C++ sources, CMake, or `.clang-tidy`, prove the org C++ guardrails still hold. Read numbers from `docs/guardrails/cpp/profile.thresholds.yml`. Do not copy those numbers into this rule.

## Prefer local CI

If the repo has `scripts/check-ci-local.sh` or `common/scripts/check-ci-local.sh`, run it. Otherwise configure with the `ci-linux` preset (binary dir `build`) and run `ctest`.

## What to check

| Topic | Guardrail |
|-------|-----------|
| C++20 via `target_compile_features` | CPP-BUILD-001, CPP-BUILD-030 |
| `FILE_SET`, `EXPORT_NAME`, `GNUInstallDirs`, hidden visibility, `SOVERSION` | CPP-BUILD-031 through CPP-BUILD-036 |
| One standard library for every linked port | CPP-BUILD-038 |
| Manifest dependency has a `find_package` | CPP-BUILD-039 |
| `<PROJ>_BUILD_TESTS` defaults to `PROJECT_IS_TOP_LEVEL` | CPP-BUILD-040 |
| `openat2` `RESOLVE_BENEATH` or a per-component `openat` walk | CPP-SEC-005 |
| Checked size arithmetic and a byte cap | CPP-SEC-006 |
| Unique compile-time table keys | CPP-GEN-004 |
| clang-tidy header filter includes the library headers | CPP-LINT-002 |
| Clang AST documentation warnings | CPP-DOC-001, CPP-DOC-004 |

Cite the Guardrail ID in the pull request when a gate fails.
